From 661a4af3ccba491f0455bbf88c0f310ed431f39d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Heyang Zhou <hello@su3.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:16:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] x86: save FS/GS before a remote TCB stall

With FSGSBASE instructions, userspace can change its hardware TLS bases without updating the saved TCB context. A syscall or interrupt may service a remote stall while waiting for the CLH lock, before c_entry_hook saves those bases. The callback replaces ksCurThread with idle and may return directly to userspace, losing the original thread bases.

Save FS/GS at the x86 stall dispatch before either callback path can switch to idle. The ordinary interrupt path may have saved them already; saving again is harmless. The existing save helper excludes VM guests. MSR-based kernels need no change.
---
 src/arch/x86/smp/ipi.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/arch/x86/smp/ipi.c b/src/arch/x86/smp/ipi.c
index 15bd8ade9..baeecb93d 100644
--- a/src/arch/x86/smp/ipi.c
+++ b/src/arch/x86/smp/ipi.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <config.h>
+#include <machine.h>
 #include <mode/smp/ipi.h>
 #include <smp/ipi.h>
 #include <smp/lock.h>
@@ -18,6 +19,13 @@ void handleRemoteCall(IpiRemoteCall_t call, word_t arg0, word_t arg1, word_t arg
     if (clh_is_ipi_pending(getCurrentCPUIndex())) {
         switch (call) {
         case IpiRemoteCall_Stall:
+#ifdef CONFIG_FSGSBASE_INST
+            /* A syscall/IRQ can service this IPI while waiting for the
+             * kernel lock, before c_entry_hook saves the user bases.
+             * Save them before the callback replaces ksCurThread with
+             * the idle thread, including its non-returning path. */
+            x86_save_fsgs_base(NODE_STATE(ksCurThread), CURRENT_CPU_INDEX());
+#endif
             ipiStallCoreCallback(irqPath);
             break;
 
